---
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">
  <channel>
    <title>{{ site.title | xml_escape }}</title>
    <description>{{ site.description | xml_escape }}</description>
    <link>{{ site.url }}{{ site.baseurl }}/</link>
    <atom:link href="{{ "/feed.xml" | absolute_url }}" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/>
    <pubDate>{{ site.time | date_to_rfc822 }}</pubDate>
    <lastBuildDate>{{ site.time | date_to_rfc822 }}</lastBuildDate>
    <generator>Jekyll v{{ jekyll.version }}</generator>
    {% comment %}
      The main feed is the current publication. It carries essays from the publication
      generation now running, newest first, and nothing else: an archived essay is not
      re-announced to subscribers because its corpus state changed, and a withdrawal
      notice is not delivered as if it were an article. Membership is the shared
      predicate in _includes/backlist.html — the same one /research/ and / use — so a
      new article enters the feed by publishing, with nothing to edit here.

      Item identity is deliberately untouched: <link> and <guid isPermaLink="true"> are
      still the article's own permanent URL and <pubDate> is still its original
      publication date, so items a reader already has keep their identity and stay read.
    {% endcomment %}
    {%- include backlist.html -%}
    {%- assign feed_posts = site.posts | where_exp: "p", "p.withdrawn != true" -%}
    {%- assign feed_emitted = 0 -%}
    {%- for post in feed_posts -%}
      {%- capture feed_key %}|{{ post.slug }}|{% endcapture -%}
      {%- unless backlist_active_slugs contains feed_key %}{% continue %}{% endunless -%}
      {% comment %} Editor's notes are not essays and are not syndicated here. They live at
        /notes/, they are excluded from the article catalogue and every article count, and
        including one would push a note published months ago into subscribers' readers as
        new material the moment the essay list grew shorter than the item limit. {% endcomment %}
      {%- if backlist_note_slugs contains feed_key %}{% continue %}{% endif -%}
      {%- if feed_emitted >= 10 %}{% break %}{% endif -%}
      {%- assign feed_emitted = feed_emitted | plus: 1 -%}
      <item>
        <title>{{ post.title | xml_escape }}</title>
        <description>{{ post.content | strip_html | truncatewords: 50 | xml_escape }}</description>
        <pubDate>{{ post.date | date_to_rfc822 }}</pubDate>
        <link>{{ post.url | absolute_url }}</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">{{ post.url | absolute_url }}</guid>
        <dc:creator>{{ site.article_credit | xml_escape }}</dc:creator>
        {% for tag in post.tags %}
          <category>{{ tag | xml_escape }}</category>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for cat in post.categories %}
          <category>{{ cat | xml_escape }}</category>
        {% endfor %}
      </item>
    {% endfor %}
  </channel>
</rss>
